<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciutadella de Menorca</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ciutadella, Iamona</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ciutadella de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Menorca</a> is a town on the western tip of Menorca in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Known in Roman times as Iamo or Iamona, it was the island's capital under Muslim rule and after the Aragonese conquest of 1287, until the British moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahon">Mahón</a> in 1722. Its old town contains a Gothic cathedral and many palaces of the Menorcan nobility.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciutadella-de-menorca.jpg" alt="Ciutadella de Menorca" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J. Braun · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudadela_(Menorca).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
